## 🐧 OverTheWire: Level 25 -> 26

### The Challenge: The Restricted Shell & The Firewall Block
**The Concept:** Level 26 doesn't use `/bin/bash`. It uses a custom script that prints ASCII art and kicks you out instantly. Plus, OverTheWire blocks all internal `localhost` connections on port 2220 to save server CPU.
**The Hack:** Bypassed the firewall by stealing the SSH key to my local PC using `scp`. Then, I zoomed in my terminal to make the text massive, forcing the `more` command to pause, allowing me to hijack the `vi` editor and spawn a real shell.
**Key Commands:**
- `scp -P 2220 bandit25@...:bandit26.sshkey D:\` (steal key to local PC)
- `icacls bandit26.sshkey /inheritance:r /grant:r %USERNAME%:R` (lock down Windows permissions)
- `ssh -i bandit26.sshkey -p 2220 bandit26@...` (connect externally to bypass localhost block)

### The Big Lesson: Environment is Everything
When `localhost` is blocked and the OS restricts your window size, you don't quit. You diagnose the infrastructure, steal the key to your own machine, and force the environment to bend to your will.

