## 🔥 Cybersecurity Masterclass: Asymmetric Encryption

| Key Type | Analogy | Who has it? |
|---|---|---|
| **Public Key** | The Padlock | Given to the server (anyone can see it) |
| **Private Key** | The Physical Key | Kept safe on your PC (never crosses the internet) |

**SSH Fingerprints:** When SSH asks to verify the "ED25519 fingerprint", you are verifying the server's Public Key. This prevents Man-in-the-Middle attacks (fake servers stealing your credentials).

